EXPERIMENT 28 – WHITE-BOX TESTING USING STATEMENT COVERAGE (JUNIT)
AIM
To write JUnit test cases to implement white-box testing using statement coverage on a number sorting program using JUnit.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the JUnit 5 junit-jupiter dependency to pom.xml.
2. Create the SortUtil class with the bubbleSort(int[] a) method.
3. Identify the statements: null check, outer loop, inner loop, comparison and three swap statements.
4. Write tests for an unsorted array, sorted array, single-element array, empty array and null array.
5. Run tests using the IDE's Run with Coverage option and verify that every statement of bubbleSort() is executed.
6. Stop.
CODE
SortUtil.java
public class SortUtil {
    public static int[] bubbleSort(int[] a) {
        if (a == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Array is null");
        }

        int n = a.length;

        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
                if (a[j] > a[j + 1]) {
                    int temp = a[j];
                    a[j] = a[j + 1];
                    a[j + 1] = temp;
                }
            }
        }
        return a;
    }
}


SortUtilTest.java
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class SortUtilTest {

    @Test
    void sortsUnsortedArray() {
        assertArrayEquals(
            new int[]{1, 2, 5, 9},
            SortUtil.bubbleSort(new int[]{5, 2, 9, 1})
        );
    }

    @Test
    void keepsSortedArrayUnchanged() {
        assertArrayEquals(
            new int[]{1, 2, 3},
            SortUtil.bubbleSort(new int[]{1, 2, 3})
        );
    }

    @Test
    void singleElementArray() {
        assertArrayEquals(
            new int[]{7},
            SortUtil.bubbleSort(new int[]{7})
        );
    }

    @Test
    void emptyArray() {
        assertArrayEquals(
            new int[]{},
            SortUtil.bubbleSort(new int[]{})
        );
    }

    @Test
    void nullArrayThrowsException() {
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class,
            () -> SortUtil.bubbleSort(null));
    }
}


INPUT
